# Keith Walker – ITAI 1371 Machine Learning Portfolio

## Course
ITAI 1371 – Introduction to Machine Learning

## About Me
My name is Keith Walker. I am interested in machine learning, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, music recommendation systems, and how AI can be used in real-world products.

This portfolio contains my labs, assignments, midterm project, and final project from ITAI 1371. Throughout the course, I practiced working with datasets, preparing data, training machine learning models, evaluating results, and reflecting on ethical issues in AI.

## Portfolio Structure
This repository is organized into three main sections:

- **Labs** – Hands-on machine learning exercises
- **Assignments** – Course assignments and written reflections
- **Projects** – Midterm and final machine learning projects

## Labs Included
- Lab 03 – Machine Learning Workflow and Types of Learning
- Lab 04 – Exploratory Data Analysis
- Lab 05 – Data Preparation
- Lab 06 – Regression and Classification
- Lab 07 – Model Evaluation
- Lab 08 – Bias-Variance Tradeoff
- Lab 10 – Unsupervised Learning
- Lab 11 – Hyperparameter Tuning and AutoML
- Lab 12 – Ethics, Fairness, and Bias

## Projects Included
- Midterm Project Topic Selection
- Midterm Project Report
- Final Project Topic Selection
- Final Project Presentation
- Final Project Report

## Tools Used
- Python
- Google Colab
- pandas
- numpy
- scikit-learn
- matplotlib
- seaborn
- AutoGluon
- GitHub

## What I Learned
This course helped me understand the full machine learning workflow, including data cleaning, model training, model evaluation, hyperparameter tuning, clustering, fairness, and project documentation. I also learned how important it is to clearly explain the purpose, process, and results of a machine learning project.
